    <meta name='title' content='odyssey.x3d'/>
    <meta name='description' content='A Material Odyssey: a 138 s film in one X3D 4.0 file. The source gift (Materials from nothing: 13 shapes, 11 materials, 4 lights, 1 interpolator) rebuilt 1:1 and intensified into a 660 m set of 35 PBR materials, 60 lights and 124 interpolators, with the director&apos;s camera (Viewpoint DroneCam) keyed at 30 keys per second. Every interpolator is clocked by TimeSensor DEF Film through ROUTEs; there is no Script node. Every albedo was generated by an image model; normal and metallicRoughness maps were derived from those images.'/>
    <meta name='creator' content='HagopJay'/>
    <meta name='created' content='11 October 2026'/>
    <meta name='generator' content='scene/build_scene.py (Python 3 + numpy) from plan/shotlist.json'/>
    <meta name='reference' content='plan/shotlist.json (the shot list: 21 shots, 171 camera keys, 58 cues)'/>
    <meta name='camera' content='CamPos/CamRot/CamFov: 4141 keys each; time-parameterised Catmull-Rom on position, view and up vectors with zero tangents at holds; fieldOfView = 2 atan(12 / lens_mm) (smaller viewport dimension)'/>
  </head>
  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title='A Material Odyssey' info='"One X3D file: the set, the materials, the lights and the director&apos;s camera. One TimeSensor DEF Film clocks every interpolator; no Script node." "Built by scene/build_scene.py from plan/shotlist.json."'/>
